# HPC

Sources: faer (views + `MemStack` scratch, defer alloc to the caller), [Numerical Computing with Rust on CPU](https://numerical-rust-cpu-81b2c3.pages.in2p3.fr/22-parasol.html) (layout, no nested Rayon), gprx design §7–§8.

- Own buffers in `Workspace`. Algorithms take `MatRef`/`MatMut` plus faer’s `MemStack`. Do not `Mat::zeros` / `Vec::new` inside the MLL/grad/predict loop. Count with `tests/alloc.rs`.
- Match faer layout: column-major. Walk columns (or blocks of columns), not rows. Kernel `uplo = Lower` so we do not fill both triangles.
- No `clone` / `to_owned` / `collect::<Vec<_>>()` on hot paths. If you need a temp, it already lives in `Workspace`.
- Do not hide `O(n²)` copies behind convenience APIs. A function that must allocate is named `to_*` and is not used in `fit` after setup.
- One Rayon pool, shared with faer. No `par_iter` inside a faer-parallel region. Split `thread_scratch` before the parallel region (design §7.1).
- `#[inline]` only after `just bench` shows it matters. Kernel SIMD lives in `src/kernel/simd/`, with one set of lane helpers in `simd/mod.rs`: isotropic RBF / Periodic / RQ for any storage (`simd/stationary.rs`), ARD RBF (`simd/rbf_ard.rs`), ARD Matérn / RQ value and `θ` derivative (`simd/ard.rs`), and squared-distance / `(Δx_d)²` row loops (`simd/dist.rs`). A leaf file calls these; it does not define its own lane helpers. Other leaves stay scalar until measured.
- Keep indices `usize`. Do not iterate with `i32` to “be like BLAS” in Rust.
- Parallel / SIMD may change bitwise results. Tests compare with tolerances, not bit-identity, unless a test is explicitly sequential.
- `f32`/`f64` mixing only at documented `PrecisionPolicy` boundaries. Do not silently `as f64` in a kernel loop.

```rust
// BAD — alloc + row-wise scrape in the optimizer loop
let k = dist.to_owned();
for i in 0..n { for j in 0..n { out[(i, j)] = f(k[(i, j)]); } }

// GOOD — reuse Workspace, lower triangle, column-friendly
kernel.apply(dist, out.rb_mut(), Triangle::Lower);
```
